{"schema":1,"language":"en","set":{"id":"swsh12tg","name":"Silver Tempest Trainer Gallery","releaseDate":"2022-11-11","cardCount":{"official":30,"total":30}},"cards":[{"id":"swsh12tg-TG01","localId":"TG01","name":"Braixen","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"When the twig is plucked from its tail, friction sets the twig alight. The flame is used to send signals to its allies."},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG02","localId":"TG02","name":"Milotic","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"Milotic has provided inspiration to many artists. It has even been referred to as the most beautiful Pokémon of all."},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG03","localId":"TG03","name":"Flaaffy","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"It stores electricity in its fluffy fleece. If it stores up too much, it will start to go bald in those patches."},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG04","localId":"TG04","name":"Jynx","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"In certain parts of Galar, Jynx was once feared and worshiped as the Queen of Ice."},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG05","localId":"TG05","name":"Gardevoir","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"It has the power to predict the future. Its power peaks when it is protecting its Trainer."},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG06","localId":"TG06","name":"Malamar","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"It's said that Malamar's hypnotic powers played a role in certain history-changing events."},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG07","localId":"TG07","name":"Rockruff","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"When it rubs the rocks on its neck against you, that's proof of its love for you. However, the rocks are sharp, so the gesture is quite painful!"},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG08","localId":"TG08","name":"Passimian","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"Passimian live in groups of about 20, with each member performing an assigned role. Through cooperation, the group survives."},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG09","localId":"TG09","name":"Druddigon","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"Druddigon are vicious and cunning. They take up residence in nests dug out by other Pokémon, treating the stolen nests as their own lairs."},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG10","localId":"TG10","name":"Smeargle","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"It draws symbols with the fluid that oozes from the tip of its tail. Depending on the symbol, Smeargle fanatics will pay big money for them."},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG11","localId":"TG11","name":"Altaria","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"description":"As it flies in a calm and relaxed manner, Altaria performs a humming song that would enrapture any audience."},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG12","localId":"TG12","name":"Kricketune V","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false}},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG13","localId":"TG13","name":"Serperior V","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false}},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG14","localId":"TG14","name":"Blaziken V","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false}},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG15","localId":"TG15","name":"Blaziken VMAX","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false}},{"id":"swsh12tg-TG16","localId":"TG16","name":"Zeraora V","variants":{"normal":false,"holo":true,"reverse":false,"firstEditio